$A$ to a chain of prime ideals of $B$. The injectivity hypothesis supplies exactly the
condition $\ker(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ A\ B) \subseteq \mathfrak p$ for every prime
$\mathfrak p$, required for lying over to apply to the bottom prime of a chain; without it the
statement is false (e.g. $\mathbb Z \to \mathbb Z/2\mathbb Z$: the extension is integral, but
$\dim \mathbb Z = 1 > 0 = \dim \mathbb Z/2\mathbb Z$).
-/
@[blueprint
  (statement := /-- If `Algebra.IsIntegral A B` and `Function.Injective (algebraMap A B)`, then `ringKrullDim A ≤ ringKrullDim B`. -/)
  (hasProof := true)
  (proof := /-- Chain lifting: given a chain of primes of $A$, lying over for the bottom prime (valid because injectivity gives $\ker(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ A\ B) \subseteq \mathfrak p_0$) and going up repeatedly produce a chain of primes of $B$ contracting onto the given chain; hence `Order.krullDim (PrimeSpectrum A) ≤ Order.krullDim (PrimeSpectrum B)`. -/)
  (proofUses := [])
  (title := /-- Dimension of the base is at most that of a faithful integral extension -/)
]
lemma ringKrullDim_ge_of_isIntegral {A B : Type} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
